meta {
  name: Create Attribute - HierarchyAttribute (500, Unimplemented)
  type: http
  seq: 8
}

post {
  url: {{pim_base_url_v3}}/product-attributes
  body: json
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}
  Content-Type: application/json
  Accept: application/json
}

body:json {
  {
    "name": "wc_test_hierarchy",
    "type": "HierarchyAttribute"
  }
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 500
}

docs {
  Confirmed live 2026-09-07. Creates nothing (server error, no resource
  produced).

  `{"data":[],"errors":[{"name":"ConfigurationError","description":"There
  was an error processing your request. Please try again later"}]}` --
  `500 Internal Server Error`.

  `HierarchyAttribute` passes pydantic's discriminator validation (it's a
  real recognized `type` tag -- see "Create Attribute - Invalid Type (422,
  Lists Undocumented Type).bru") but the actual create handler isn't wired
  up for it. Reads as a work-in-progress/unfinished feature flag rather
  than a documented bug -- **do not build customer-facing docs around
  this type**, and flag it to Plytix as: (a) confirmation it's
  intentionally hidden/unfinished, not a live bug worth a support ticket,
  and (b) a nudge to keep `openapi_pimv3.json`'s `oneOf` in sync once (if)
  it does ship.
}
